#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bit_not

#% text
# `bit_not(n)` gives the bitwise complement of the integer `n`, `-1 - n`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The integers are taken in two's complement with infinitely many leading bits, so the complement of a non-negative integer is negative.

#% item
# `bit_not` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bit_not(0)
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
bit_not(5)
#% output
#= -6

#% cell
bit_not(-6)
#% output
#= 5

#% cell
bit_not([1, 2, 3])
#% output
#= [-2, -3, -4]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Complementing twice gives the integer back:

#% cell
bit_not(bit_not(2026))
#% output
#= 2026

#% text
# Clearing bits with `bit_and` and the complement of a mask:

#% cell
bit_and(255, bit_not(15))
#% output
#= 240

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bit_and`, `bit_or`, `bit_xor`
